{#
  The assignment edit form — the Twig counterpart of
  module/Schoenstatt/view/schoenstatt/assignments/edit.phtml and its fields-partial.phtml.

  **The first ported page with a delete-confirmation modal**, which is a *second* form on
  the page. Three things about it are load-bearing:

  - It is gated on `route/assignments/assignment/delete`, a different permission from the
    one that let the visitor reach this page — `sch_general_moderator` against
    `sch_moderator`. Both the trigger button and the modal are inside that gate, and both
    have to be, or a moderator gets a button that opens a modal that posts to a 403.
  - Its action is the **laminas** delete route. This batch ports the edit verb only, so the
    modal is a Symfony-rendered form posting to a bridged URL. Its CSRF token is accepted
    there because both front controllers read the same laminas session.
  - `EditAssignmentForm::prepareforEdit()` disables `associationId`, `roleId` and
    `personId`, so the three selects render greyed out — an assignment's *who* and *where*
    are fixed once created, and only its dates are editable. That happens in the form
    factory, not here.

  The "New person?" paragraph is gated the same way the library form's is, and is inside a
  further condition: it only shows when `personId` is *not* disabled, which on this edit
  page it always is. So the paragraph never renders here — reproduced anyway, because the
  same partial serves the create page where it does.

  **The field rows live in `schoenstatt/_assignment-fields.html.twig` now**, shared with the create
  form so that a field cannot be added to one surface and quietly forgotten on the
  other. What stays in this file is what edit.phtml keeps outside its own partial —
  which is not the same set for every entity, and is the detail worth checking before
  moving anything across the boundary.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('schoenstatt/_assignment-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{% if is_allowed('route/assignments/assignment/delete') %}
&nbsp;{{ form_button(form.get('delete')) }}
{% endif %}
{{ form_close() }}

{% if is_allowed('route/assignments/assignment/delete') %}
<!-- Modal -->
<div class="modal fade bs-example-modal-sm" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="mySmallModalLabel">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-sm">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"><span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span></button>
        <h4 class="modal-title">{{ translate('Careful') }}...</h4>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>{{ translate('Only delete an assignment if it was created by mistake!
        		If you wish change the person in charge, simply set an "End Date" in the past
        		and create a new assignment.') }}</p>
{{ form_open(delete_form, delete_action) }}
{{ form_row(delete_form.get('security')) }}
{{ form_submit(delete_form.get('submit')) }}
&nbsp;{{ form_button(delete_form.get('cancel')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
